 "notes": [
  "Main source: CRC 'Regulatory policy for civil radio-spectrum management 2025-2027' (CRC decision 213, 26 June 2025), which gives the current layouts for 900 MHz, 2.6 GHz, 3.6 GHz and 26 GHz and amounts for 1800/2100 MHz.",
  "The CRC figures for 2.6 GHz and 3.6 GHz do not name operators per block; operator order comes from the davwheat seed (single source), hence 'unverified'.",
  "3400-3430 MHz is marked 'occupied' in the CRC figure without a holder; it is not drawn.",
  "26 GHz totals include blocks held under converted fixed-service permits (Yettel/A1) that may be used for MFCN; Yettel 880 MHz, A1 740 MHz, Vivacom 600 MHz, MoD 112 MHz.",
  "Seed 800/700 MHz notes about restrictions until end-2025 relate to military radar 'sanitary zones' (Council of Ministers decision 699/2023).",
  "Coverage badge lowered from \"Positions verified\" to \"Holdings only\" by the atlas-wide rule (block-level = every counted band verified; positions verified ≥ 60%; partial = a required band's status is unknown)."
 ],
 "missing": [
  "Per-operator block positions at 1800 and 2100 MHz and the operator order at 2.6/3.6 GHz confirmed only by the seed.",
  "Expiry dates for 900/1800 MHz and 3.6/26 GHz permits (the CRC permit register lists dates per permit number but not per band).",
  "Holder of 3400-3430 MHz.",
  "Carrier EARFCN/NR-ARFCN details beyond a few seed notes."
 ],
 "changes": [
  "2100 MHz: fixed the seed's Vivacom uplink 1960-1970 (DL/UL width mismatch) to 1960-1980; CRC confirms 2x20 MHz each; expiry 25 Apr 2035 added.",
  "900 MHz and 26 GHz marked 'verified' against the CRC policy figures; 1800, 2100, 2600 and 3.6 GHz downgraded to 'unverified' (seed-only positions).",
  "26 GHz: merged adjacent same-operator blocks and made the 24250-24300 edge a guard band.",
  "3.6 GHz: removed the seed's 'unassigned' 3400-3430 (CRC says occupied) and kept 3430-3440 as free.",
  "Operator names shortened to brands (A1, Yettel, Vivacom); MoD set to kind 'government'.",
  "Added not-assigned entries for 600, 850, 1400, 1700, 1900, 2000tdd, 2300, 2600 TDD, 4900, 40g, 47g."
 ],
